# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: make-test-loads-installed-clautolisp -- the test images run an INSTALLED copy instead of the checkout when ASDF's inherited registry can see one
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-make-test-loads-installed-clautolisp
#+DATE: 2026-11-19

* Symptom

poseidon (Debian, SBCL 2.5.2, bundled ASDF 3.3.1), checkout at 99a72e48
(2.4.33), clautolisp 2.4.16 installed under /opt/local: the root =make test=
failed CADOR-SUITE with 41 failures, among them

- =GETCNAME-UNDER-A-LOCALE-WITHOUT-A-TABLE-IS-THE-IDENTITY=:
  =(cador-getcname "_LINE" :autocad locale)= => NIL instead of "LINE";
- =GETCNAME-FOLLOWS-EACH-PRODUCT-UNDER-FR-FR=,
  =GETCNAME-BRICSCAD-V26-SPELLS-STRETCH-WITH-ITS-ACCENT=;
- =NEW-DOCUMENT-USES-THE-TEMPLATE-THE-SYSVAR-NAMES= ("no bundled template"),
  =NEW-DOCUMENT-TEMPLATE-RESOLVES-A-RELATIVE-NAME-AGAINST-TEMPLATEPATH=,
  =STARTUP-DOCUMENT-FOLLOWS-THE-ENVIRONMENT-NOT-THE-SYSVAR=;
- =COMMAND-NEW-OPEN-AND-MENULOAD-NOTIFY-THE-UI= (2 documents, expected 3).

The same =make test= passed on thalassa (macOS), pfenny (Windows) and in
GitLab CI, and the binary built on poseidon was fine. Because the job looked
like an ordinary test failure, it blocked the 2.4.33 install.

* Cause

The suite was not testing the checkout. It was testing the INSTALLED sources
under /opt/local/share/common-lisp/source/clautolisp/, which have neither
=cador/data/= nor =drawing/template/= (see
=install-libraries-omits-runtime-data-files=). So the getcname tables
compiled empty, and =drawing-template-path= named a file that does not
exist.

1. Every test lane does =(asdf:load-asd <checkout>/clautolisp.asd)=, then
   =asdf:test-system=. =asdf:find-system= (ASDF 3.3, =find-system.lisp=)
   calls =locate-system=, which runs =search-for-system-definition=:
   the source-registry is searched BEFORE the already-registered system is
   considered. When the registry's .asd path differs from the registered
   one, =find-system= calls =load-asd= on the REGISTRY's file. An explicit
   =load-asd= therefore does not stick: the first =find-system= replaces it
   with whatever the source-registry finds.
2. On poseidon the user's shell sets =XDG_DATA_DIRS=/opt/local/share= (rc
   =monolith.bash=). ASDF's default registry then includes
   =/opt/local/share/common-lisp/systems/= (the =clautolisp.asd= symlink
   that =make install-libraries= creates) and the =source/= tree. As a side
   effect, =/usr/share= leaves the registry too, so Debian's ASDF is not
   self-upgraded and the image stays on 3.3.1. That is irrelevant here: 3.3.7
   behaves the same.
3. thalassa has the same data-less installed copy but never failed, because
   =~/.config/common-lisp/source-registry.conf= there says
   =:ignore-inherited-configuration=, so XDG_DATA_DIRS is never consulted.
   CI hosts have nothing installed. Anyone who follows
   =50-clautolisp.conf='s own advice (=XDG_CONFIG_DIRS=/opt/local/etc=) gets
   the same failure.

Evidence on poseidon:
- In the user's fasl cache, the installed copy's =cador/tests/=,
  =drawing/source/persistence.fasl= and =tools/clautolisp/tests/run.fasl=
  were compiled during the failing run (10:57-10:58), interleaved with the
  checkout's fasls.
- Probe: after the lanes' preamble and =load-asd=,
  =(asdf:system-source-directory "clautolisp/cador/tests")= is the checkout
  when XDG_DATA_DIRS is unset, and
  =/opt/local/share/common-lisp/source/clautolisp/= when it is
  =/opt/local/share=. The same holds under ASDF 3.3.7.3.
- In a copy of this branch, with =XDG_DATA_DIRS=/opt/local/share=:
  =make test-sbcl TEST_SYSTEM=clautolisp/cador/tests CHECKOUT_REGISTRY_LOAD==
  (the fix switched off) gives *2262/2303, 41 failures*. The same command
  with the fix gives *2307/2307*.

Measured on poseidon: a bare =ssh poseidon 'cmd'= environment has no
XDG_DATA_DIRS, while an interactive shell, and =ssh poseidon bash -s=, have
=/opt/local/share=. That would explain why some earlier checks there
("the cador suite alone passes", "every system resolves to the checkout")
came out clean.

The build had the same flaw, in a smaller form.
=configure-asdf-directories= (=generate.lisp=) put the checkout first, but
as a non-recursive =:directory=. So =tui-core.asd= and
=clautolisp-tui-curses.asd=, which live in subdirectories, still came from
the default registry, that is from the installed copy. In addition,
=generate-clautolisp.lisp= pre-loaded =clautolisp-tui-curses= BEFORE
configuring the registry at all. The 2.4.33 binary built on poseidon is
nevertheless correct: those two directories are byte-identical between the
installed 2.4.16 copy and the 2.4.33 checkout (=diff -rq=).

* Fix (2.4.34)

- =clautolisp/tools/checkout-source-registry.lisp=: re-initialises the
  source-registry with this tree first (=:tree= of the clautolisp subproject
  minus =third-party/=, =build/= and =.cache/=, then
  =autolisp-front-end/= and =autolisp-test/= as =:directory=), then
  =:inherit-configuration=. The first entry that names a system wins, so
  third-party systems still come from wherever they came from. Paths come
  from =*load-truename*=, never from a Makefile.
- Loaded right after =(require :asdf)= by every image that =load-asd='s
  the checkout:
  - clautolisp =test-sbcl=, =test-ccl=, =test-ecl= (=CHECKOUT_REGISTRY_LOAD=);
  - =whole-suite-compiled.lisp=, =whole-suite-lexical.lisp=,
    =debug-suite-compiled.lisp=, =check-docstrings.lisp=;
  - the alfe Makefile lanes (=test-sbcl=, =test-ccl=, =conformance=);
  - the autolisp-test =test-asdf-*= lanes.
- Build: =configure-asdf-directories= scans each directory as a =:tree=
  (same exclusions). =generate-clautolisp.lisp= configures the registry
  before its tui-curses pre-load.
- Regression test =make -C clautolisp test-checkout-registry=, run first by
  =make test= (=tools/checkout-source-registry-test.lisp=). It plants a
  decoy install (=clautolisp.asd= with =clautolisp/cador= and
  =clautolisp/cador/tests=, =tui-core.asd=, =clautolisp-tui-curses.asd=,
  =autolisp-front-end.asd=) in a scratch dir under XDG_CACHE_HOME and makes
  the inherited registry see it through =CL_SOURCE_REGISTRY=, which
  outranks a user conf file such as thalassa's. It then checks that the
  inherited registry alone finds the decoy, so the test is not vacuous, and
  that after the fix and the lanes' =load-asd= every one of those systems,
  plus the drawing template, resolves into the checkout. With the fix
  emptied it reports 8 failures. With the fix it passes on thalassa and
  poseidon.

* Not covered (no =make test= lane uses them)

=scripts/verify-vl-registry.lisp=, =scripts/verify-pathname-mapping.lisp=,
=scripts/test-vendor-templates.sh=,
=autolisp-front-end/scripts/check-spec-coverage.lisp=,
=clautolisp/tools/generate-dialect-warnings-annex.lisp=,
=run-file-compat/launch.lisp= and the tui-curses =test/*.lisp= still
=load-asd= without the registry file. They can be fixed the same way when
they are next touched.

* Interim workaround for an unfixed checkout

#+begin_src sh
env -u XDG_DATA_DIRS -u XDG_CONFIG_DIRS -u CL_SOURCE_REGISTRY ~/update-clautolisp
#+end_src

* Resolved

2026-11-19, clautolisp 2.4.34 / alfe 2.4.34, branch
=fix-make-test-loads-installed-clautolisp=. =test-checkout-registry= also
runs in both CIs (=test:clautolisp:sbcl= and its ci.yml mirror). Verified
as follows:
- thalassa, =make -C clautolisp test=: 34 suites, 13913 checks, 0 failures.
- poseidon (copy of the branch, =XDG_DATA_DIRS=/opt/local/share=):
  =test-checkout-registry= PASS, cador suite 2307/2307.
- pfenny (Windows, copy of the branch): =test-checkout-registry= PASS. The
  decoy environment is set by the Makefile, because =(setf uiop:getenv)=
  fails on Windows SBCL.
